    "created_at": "2026-03-26T19:07:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-26T19:07:58Z",
    "body": "Hi @tdegrunt, thanks for the thorough report and the VS Code comparison!\n\nA few follow-up questions to help us nail down the full scope of the fix:\n\n1. After you renamed `credsStore` → `credStore`, did credentials get stored **via the credential helper** (the UUID-named binary), or in **plaintext** inside `~/.docker/config.json`? This matters because VS Code also injects a credential helper binary into the container — Zed may be missing that step too.\n2. Does the `docker-credential-dev-containers-<UUID>` binary exist anywhere in the container's PATH after Zed sets up the devcontainer?\n3. Does this happen with Docker Desktop instead of OrbStack?\n\nThe root cause is likely a typo in Zed's devcontainer setup code (`credsStore` vs. `credStore`). Thanks!",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
